    <node id="GENETIC COUNSELOR">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A genetic counselor is a health professional with specialized training in genetic diseases and cancer genetics. They help patients understand gene changes related to disease and hereditary cancer risk, and assist individuals in deciding whether to undergo germline testing. In addition, genetic counselors interpret the results of genetic tests, providing expert guidance and counseling. They may also provide counseling as recommended by the National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) for people with a genetic risk of skin cancer. Overall, genetic counselors support patients in making informed decisions about genetic testing and understanding the implications of their genetic test results.
Relationships:
  - Source: GENETIC TESTING
  - Target: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Description: Genetic testing may be done through a genetic counselor, who helps patients understand the results
  - Source: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Target: GENETIC TESTING
  - Description: A genetic counselor helps interpret the results of genetic tests
  - Source: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Target: MEDICAL PROVIDERS
  - Description: Medical providers and genetic counselors can both be consulted about family cancer history.
  - Source: CARE TEAM
  - Target: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Description: The care team can help a patient access a genetic counselor
  - Source: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Target: PATIENT
  - Description: The patient can talk to a genetic counselor about testing decisions and results.
  - Source: OVARIAN CANCER
  - Target: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Description: A genetic counselor helps patients with ovarian cancer and cancer family history understand genetic risk
  - Source: DOCTOR
  - Target: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Description: A doctor can refer a patient to a genetic counselor.
  - Source: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Target: GERMLINE TESTING
  - Description: A genetic counselor helps patients decide about germline testing and interprets results
  - Source: GERMLINE TESTING
  - Target: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Description: A genetic counselor helps patients decide whether to undergo germline testing and interpret the results.
  - Source: GENETIC TEST
  - Target: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Description: A genetic counselor helps patients decide on and interpret genetic tests.
  - Source: NCCN
  - Target: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Description: NCCN recommends that patients with a genetic risk of skin cancer receive counseling from specialists such as genetic counselors.
  - Source: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Target: GENETIC COUNSELING
  - Description: A genetic counselor is the professional who provides genetic counseling
  - Source: FINDAGENETICCOUNSELOR.COM
  - Target: GENETIC COUNSELOR
  - Description: findageneticcounselor.com is a website used to find a genetic counselor</data>
