      <data key="d4">ENTITY: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
Description: Platinum chemotherapy is a type of cancer treatment that uses drugs containing the metal platinum. This category includes well-known agents such as cisplatin and carboplatin. It is commonly administered during radiation therapy, often concurrently with external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) as part of a chemoradiation regimen. This approach is specifically utilized in the treatment of cancers such as squamous cell skin cancer and cervical cancer, among others. As a systemic therapy, platinum chemotherapy works by interfering with DNA replication in rapidly dividing cancer cells, enhancing the effects of radiation when given together.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Platinum chemotherapy is a type of chemotherapy.

  - Source: PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Platinum-based chemotherapy includes platinum chemotherapy drugs.

  - Source: EBRT
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Platinum chemotherapy may be administered with external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) as part of chemoradiation.

  - Source: SYSTEMIC THERAPY
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Platinum chemotherapy is a systemic therapy.

---</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADJUVANT THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Adjuvant therapy is a systemic drug treatment administered after surgery, also referred to as postoperative therapy. It is given following primary treatment—such as surgical removal of a tumor—with the goal of lowering the risk that the cancer will return. In addition to systemic drugs, radiation therapy may also be used as adjuvant therapy after surgery.
Relationships:
  - Source: ADJUVANT THERAPY
  - Target: SYSTEMIC THERAPY
  - Description: Adjuvant therapy is a systemic drug treatment given after surgery
  - Source: ADJUVANT THERAPY
  - Target: CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Chemotherapy can be given as adjuvant therapy after surgery
  - Source: ADJUVANT THERAPY
  - Target: RADIATION THERAPY
  - Description: Radiation therapy may also be used as adjuvant therapy after surgery</data>
