    <node id="SMOKEFREE.GOV">
      <data key="d3">11</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">SMOKEFREE.GOV is an online quit-smoking resource and support website recommended to help people stop smoking or vaping. It is specifically designed as a smoking-cessation tool, offering support and guidance for individuals who smoke or vape and want to quit. The resource is frequently referenced as a trusted online destination for those seeking help to overcome nicotine addiction, providing accessible information and encouragement to support users through the quitting process.
Relationships:
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: SMOKING
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov is designed for people who smoke and want support quitting
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: QUITTING SMOKING
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov is listed as an online support resource to help people quit smoking
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: VAPING
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov is also recommended as support for people who vape
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov and BeTobaccoFree.gov are two online support websites that are listed together as recommended resources for individuals seeking help to quit smoking, tobacco use, and vaping. Both are highlighted as trusted digital cessation support options, offering guidance and tools for those ready to stop using tobacco products or e-cigarettes.
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: BETOBACCOFREE
  - Description: Both are listed together in the text as online support websites for quitting smoking or vaping
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov and CDC.gov/tobacco are both recognized as recommended online resources for quitting smoking and vaping. They are frequently listed together as credible, web-based smoking cessation support options, providing individuals with accessible tools and information to help them stop using tobacco products or e-cigarettes. Both websites serve as authoritative sources of guidance for those seeking to quit.
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: CANCER TREATMENT
  - Description: Stopping smoking or vaping is essential to maximize the chance of cure and minimize side effects from cancer treatment; SmokeFree.gov is an online resource to help quit.
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: PATIENT
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov is an online support resource for the patient to quit smoking or vaping
  - Source: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Target: CDC
  - Description: SmokeFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, SmokeFree.gov is listed as an online support option to help people quit smoking or vaping, while the CDC’s website, CDC.gov/tobacco, is also listed as an online support resource for quitting tobacco. Together, they serve as accessible digital tools for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and assistance to those looking to stop using tobacco products.
  - Source: CDC.GOV/TOBACCO
  - Target: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Description: Both are recommended online smoking/vaping cessation support resources.
  - Source: BETOBACCOFREE.GOV
  - Target: SMOKEFREE.GOV
  - Description: Both are recommended online smoking/vaping cessation support resources.</data>
