    <node id="INTERNATIONAL FEDERATION OF GYNECOLOGY AND OBSTETRICS">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics (FIGO) is a professional organization best known for developing the FIGO staging system, a standardized framework used to classify the extent of gynecological cancers. This system is widely adopted in clinical practice and is considered the most commonly used staging method for both ovarian cancer and cervical cancer. For ovarian cancer, the FIGO staging system is similar to the AJCC (American Joint Committee on Cancer) system, and it serves as the primary tool for determining disease progression and guiding treatment decisions. For cervical cancer, FIGO similarly provides the definitive staging criteria, ensuring consistent evaluation and communication among healthcare providers worldwide. By establishing these staging systems, FIGO has played a central role in advancing the diagnosis, treatment, and research of gynecologic malignancies. Its staging classifications are integral to oncology practice, enabling accurate prognosis and comparison of treatment outcomes across different clinical settings.
Relationships:
  - None listed</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
