    <node id="GERMLINE MUTATION">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A germline mutation is a gene mutation inherited from a birth parent. It is an inherited mutation present in every cell of the body and is passed down in families, which is why it is also called a hereditary mutation. Germline mutations can increase an individual's cancer risk, can be passed on to children, and may also be present in blood relatives.
Relationships:
  - Source: GERMLINE MUTATION
  - Target: HEREDITARY GENE TESTING
  - Description: Hereditary gene testing looks for inherited germline mutations in every cell</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
