    <node id="RELATIONSHIP: GENETIC TEST → GERMLINE TESTING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">GENETIC TEST is a broad category of medical analysis used to identify changes in chromosomes, genes, or proteins. GERMLINE TESTING is a specific form of GENETIC TEST that focuses on inherited cancer risk, meaning it looks for genetic mutations present from birth that may predispose an individual to certain cancers. In the context of prostate cancer care, GERMLINE TESTING is recognized as one of the two basic types of genetic tests used, alongside somatic testing (which examines tumor tissue). As such, GERMLINE TESTING serves both to assess hereditary cancer susceptibility and to guide treatment decisions for prostate cancer, making it a key tool in precision oncology.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">ENTITY: RELATIONSHIP: GENETIC TEST → GERMLINE TESTING
Description: GENETIC TEST is a broad category of medical analysis used to identify changes in chromosomes, genes, or proteins. GERMLINE TESTING is a specific form of GENETIC TEST that focuses on inherited cancer risk, meaning it looks for genetic mutations present from birth that may predispose an individual to certain cancers. In the context of prostate cancer care, GERMLINE TESTING is recognized as one of the two basic types of genetic tests used, alongside somatic testing (which examines tumor tissue). As such, GERMLINE TESTING serves both to assess hereditary cancer susceptibility and to guide treatment decisions for prostate cancer, making it a key tool in precision oncology.</data>
    </node>
