    <node id="BREAST CANCER">
      <data key="d3">7</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Breast cancer is a disease that starts in the cells of the breast. It often begins in the milk ducts or lobules and can spread into surrounding tissue. Breast cancer can be invasive, meaning it has the ability to spread through the lymphatic system or blood to other parts of the body. Most breast cancers are carcinomas, with the common types being ductal carcinoma and lobular carcinoma. Anyone can develop breast cancer, regardless of gender or other factors. Testing is performed on the cancer to help determine an appropriate treatment plan.
Relationships: None listed.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d4">ENTITY: BREAST CANCER
Description: Breast cancer is a disease that starts in the cells of the breast. It often begins in the milk ducts or lobules and can spread into surrounding tissue. Breast cancer can be invasive, meaning it has the ability to spread through the lymphatic system or blood to other parts of the body. Most breast cancers are carcinomas, with the common types being ductal carcinoma and lobular carcinoma. Anyone can develop breast cancer, regardless of gender or other factors. Testing is performed on the cancer to help determine an appropriate treatment plan.
Relationships: None listed.</data>
    </node>
