    <node id="MISMATCH REPAIR TESTING">
      <data key="d3">4</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Mismatch repair testing is a laboratory analysis performed on a sample of colon tumor tissue. It is used to detect the presence of mismatch repair deficiency (dMMR) or high microsatellite instability (MSI-H) biomarkers. This testing is recommended for everyone diagnosed with colon cancer, as it provides important information about the tumor's characteristics.
Relationships:
  - Source: MISMATCH REPAIR TESTING
  - Target: LYNCH SYNDROME
  - Description: If colon cancer is dMMR/MSI-H, mismatch repair testing leads to testing for Lynch syndrome
  - Source: MISMATCH REPAIR TESTING
  - Target: MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY TESTING
  - Description: Mismatch repair testing and microsatellite instability testing are recommended methods for evaluating colon cancer biomarkers
  - Source: MISMATCH REPAIR TESTING
  - Target: COLON CANCER
  - Description: All colon cancers should be tested for mismatch repair deficiency or MSI-H.
  - Source: COLON CANCER
  - Target: MISMATCH REPAIR TESTING
  - Description: All colon cancers should be tested for mismatch repair mutations; mismatch repair testing is recommended for everyone diagnosed with colon cancer</data>
