      <data key="d4">ENTITY: ECHOCARDIOGRAM
Description: An echocardiogram (echo) is a diagnostic test that uses sound waves to create pictures of the heart. It is a type of ultrasound, specifically used to image the beating heart. The test shows both the structure and the function of the heart, including its valves, muscle thickness, and important functional measures such as ejection fraction.
