    <node id="MONITORING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">MONITORING refers to the ongoing observation of a patient as part of follow-up care after treatment. It encompasses a follow-up observation strategy designed to watch for cancer recurrence or progression, which may include a watch-and-wait approach or regular testing. This process ensures that any changes in the patient's condition are detected in a timely manner, allowing for appropriate interventions if necessary. Overall, monitoring is a critical component of post-treatment care, focused on surveillance and early detection of any signs of disease returning or advancing.
Relationships: (No explicit relationships listed in the provided data for this entity.)

