    <node id="RELATIONSHIP: IMAGING → CT SCAN">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Imaging encompasses various diagnostic techniques, including the CT scan (computed tomography scan). A CT scan is an imaging test that combines multiple x-ray images to create a detailed three-dimensional picture of internal structures. In clinical practice, CT is one of the imaging tests used in surveillance after recurrence treatment, allowing healthcare providers to monitor patients for signs of recurrence and assess response to therapy.

---</data>
