    <node id="PERFORMANCE STATUS">
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Performance status (PS) is a clinical rating of a person’s general level of fitness and overall functional ability, specifically reflecting how well they can perform ordinary day-to-day activities and self-care tasks. It is commonly measured using the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) scale, which provides a standardized scoring system for a patient’s current physical capabilities. Performance status is used by the care team as part of the patient workup to help guide treatment decisions, including determining the appropriate treatment level and eligibility for clinical trials. Thus, it serves as a key indicator of a patient’s ability to carry out daily activities and informs the selection of a personalized treatment plan.
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.</data>
