    <node id="DENTAL EXAM">
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A dental exam is recommended prior to undergoing head and neck cancer treatment, as such treatment can significantly affect the health of the jaw, teeth, and gums. This dental evaluation is an important preparatory step, often including imaging such as an x-ray (Panorex) or a CT scan without contrast, to assess the condition of the oral structures. The examination is essential because head and neck cancer treatment—such as radiation therapy or surgery—can have direct impacts on the jaw, potentially leading to complications like osteoradionecrosis or other dental and periodontal issues. By identifying existing dental problems and planning necessary interventions beforehand, the dental exam helps optimize oral health and minimize treatment-related risks, ensuring better overall outcomes for the patient.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: DENTAL EXAM
  - Target: (No explicit relationship records provided in the data tables for this entity beyond the description)

---</data>
