Relationships:
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: LIVER CANCER
  - Description: Cirrhosis is a major risk factor for the development of liver cancer. It is formally listed as a risk factor for liver cancer, and clinical comparisons are often made between individuals who have cirrhosis and those who do not, highlighting the elevated risk associated with the condition. In this context, cirrhosis and liver cancer are closely linked, with cirrhosis representing a significant predisposing condition for the onset of liver cancer.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: HEPATITIS B
  - Description: Hepatitis B virus or infection can cause cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: HEPATITIS
  - Description: Hepatitis can cause cirrhosis.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: LIVER CANCER SCREENING
  - Description: People with cirrhosis should be enrolled in a liver cancer screening program.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: LIVER DISEASE
  - Description: Cirrhosis is a type of chronic liver disease.
  - Source: CIRRHOSIS
  - Target: ALPHA-1-ANTITRYPSIN DEFICIENCY
  - Description: Alpha-1-antitrypsin deficiency is listed as a cause of cirrhosis.</data>
