    <node id="MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">MSI-H/dMMR mutation is a tumor characteristic defined by the presence of high microsatellite instability (MSI-H) or deficient mismatch repair (dMMR). This mutation status occurs when errors or defects in the DNA mismatch repair system are present and are not corrected, leading to the accumulation of mutations, particularly in microsatellite regions of the genome. As a result, tumors with MSI-H/dMMR exhibit a distinct genetic profile that is clinically significant. This mutation status is relevant to biomarker testing, as it helps identify patients who may respond to certain treatments. Specifically, pembrolizumab, an immune checkpoint inhibitor, is often used to treat tumors that are MSI-H or dMMR, regardless of their location in the body. In summary, MSI-H/dMMR mutation represents a key predictive biomarker in oncology, guiding treatment decisions and enabling targeted immunotherapy for affected patients.
Relationships:
  - Source: MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION
  - Target: MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY
  - Description: MSI-H/dMMR mutation is a type of DNA change that leads to microsatellite instability-high or deficient mismatch repair. Microsatellite instability is a characteristic feature of MSI-H/dMMR mutation. In other words, the MSI-H/dMMR mutation drives the development of microsatellite instability, making the two closely related in the context of genomic alterations.
  - Source: MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION
  - Target: DEFICIENT MISMATCH REPAIR
  - Description: Deficient mismatch repair is a cause or component of MSI-H/dMMR mutation
  - Source: MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION
  - Target: MSI-H
  - Description: MSI-H is a form of MSI-H/dMMR mutation
  - Source: MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY (MSI)
  - Target: MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION
  - Description: MSI-H is high microsatellite instability, often due to dMMR genes, and is part of the MSI-H/dMMR tumor mutation status.
  - Source: DEFICIENT MISMATCH REPAIR (DMMR)
  - Target: MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION
  - Description: MSI-H/dMMR mutation includes deficient mismatch repair.
  - Source: BIOMARKER TESTING
  - Target: MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION
  - Description: Biomarker testing can identify MSI-H/dMMR mutation status
  - Source: MUTATION
  - Target: MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION
  - Description: MSI-H/dMMR mutation is a type of mutation
  - Source: MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION
  - Target: TMB-H
  - Description: Both TMB-H and MSI-H/dMMR are tumor mutation statuses that may guide treatment with immunotherapy drugs.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">9</data>
