    <node id="BCR::ABL1">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">BCR::ABL1 is an abnormal fusion gene created by the same chromosomal translocation that produces the Philadelphia chromosome; it encodes a protein that leads to uncontrolled blood cell growth and ultimately CML.
Relationships:
  - Source: CHRONIC MYELOID LEUKEMIA
  - Target: BCR::ABL1
  - Description: BCR::ABL1 produces a protein that leads to uncontrolled blood cell growth, ultimately causing CML.
  - Source: PHILADELPHIA CHROMOSOME
  - Target: BCR::ABL1
  - Description: Both are formed from the same translocation between chromosome 9 and chromosome 22: BCR::ABL1 is the fused gene, and the Philadelphia chromosome is the resulting abnormal chromosome 22.</data>
