    <node id="NEUROLOGICAL EXAM">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A neurological exam is a test used to assess brain and nervous system function, particularly in diagnosing primary CNS lymphoma. It consists of simple tests that evaluate alertness, thinking, balance, coordination, reflexes, strength, hearing, and the senses of touch and smell, and it may also include an eye exam.
Relationships:
  - Source: DIAGNOSIS
  - Target: NEUROLOGICAL EXAM
  - Description: A neurological exam is used in the diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma
  - Source: NEUROLOGICAL EXAM
  - Target: CARE TEAM
  - Description: The care team uses neurological exam results together with imaging and other assessments.
  - Source: NEUROLOGICAL EXAM
  - Target: IMAGING
  - Description: Neurological symptoms found during an exam can prompt imaging to look for a brain tumor.
  - Source: NEUROLOGICAL EXAM
  - Target: PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA
  - Description: A neurological exam is one of the important tests to confirm primary CNS lymphoma
  - Source: NEUROLOGICAL EXAM
  - Target: EYE EXAM
  - Description: An eye exam may be performed as part of the neurological exam to check optic-nerve health.</data>
