      <data key="d1">WBRT (whole brain radiation therapy) is a radiation therapy technique used to treat primary CNS lymphoma by radiating the whole brain. It can be expanded to include the eyes or replaced by focused eye radiation, and may cause vision problems, cataracts, memory problems, slowed thinking, and trouble speaking.
