    <node id="TRANSVAGINAL ULTRASOUND">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Transvaginal ultrasound is a type of imaging test in which a probe is inserted into the vagina. This approach allows the doctor to see the ovaries more clearly than with some other methods. It is also used as an alternative when a pelvic MRI cannot be performed. In the context of cervical cancer, transvaginal ultrasound may be used as part of initial imaging, and it serves as an initial imaging test to determine the extent of the disease before treatment begins.
Relationships:
  - Source: ULTRASOUND
  - Target: TRANSVAGINAL ULTRASOUND
  - Description: Transvaginal ultrasound is one of the two types of ultrasound used for ovarian cancer.

---</data>
