    <node id="TEST RESULTS">
      <data key="d3">14</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">TEST RESULTS are the consolidated findings obtained through a comprehensive diagnostic workup for nasopharyngeal cancer. These results integrate information gathered from multiple sources, including the patient's medical history, a physical examination, blood tests, imaging studies, and a biopsy. Medical history and physical examination provide initial clinical context and identify suspicious signs or symptoms, while blood tests offer additional laboratory data to support the diagnosis. Imaging studies help visualize the extent and location of the tumor, and a biopsy provides definitive tissue confirmation of malignancy. Altogether, these test results are the critical outcomes that determine the treatment plan for nasopharyngeal cancer, guiding clinical decisions regarding therapy. The information from all these diagnostic components is synthesized to establish the stage of the disease and tailor the most appropriate management strategy for the patient.
Relationships:
  - Source: TESTING FOR NPC
  - Target: TEST RESULTS
  - Description: The testing chapter covers test results and their use in treatment planning</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
