      <data key="d1">A screening mammogram is a mammogram performed on a regular basis for routine screening purposes, specifically when there are no signs or symptoms of breast cancer. It is referenced as distinct from a diagnostic mammogram, which is typically used to evaluate abnormalities or symptoms. The screening mammogram is designed to detect breast cancer early in asymptomatic individuals, and it is a routine preventive measure.
