    <node id="COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY (CT) SCAN">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY (CT) SCAN is an imaging test that combines a computer with an X-ray machine to produce detailed, three-dimensional pictures of tissues and organs inside the body. In the context of cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma (CSCC), a CT scan is specifically recommended to evaluate lymph nodes near the affected area after a biopsy has confirmed regional spread of the disease. Thus, it serves both as a general diagnostic imaging tool and as a targeted method for assessing lymph node involvement in CSCC cases.
Relationships:
  - Source: CT (COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY) SCAN
  - Target: FDG-PET/CT
  - Description: FDG-PET/CT includes CT imaging as part of the PET/CT procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
