    <node id="EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT) is a form of radiation therapy used to treat cancer. It works by directing a beam of radiation at the tumor from a machine located outside the body. In this approach, the radiation is delivered externally, targeting cancerous cells while sparing surrounding healthy tissue as much as possible.
Relationships:
  - Source: EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)
  - Target: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Description: Vaginal brachytherapy may be given in addition to EBRT</data>
