    <node id="INTENSITY-MODULATED RADIATION THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT) is an advanced type of external beam radiation therapy that uses many small beams of different strengths, or intensities, to precisely target a tumor. This technique delivers a high dose of radiation directly to the tumor while significantly reducing radiation exposure to surrounding normal tissues, such as the bowel, bladder, external genitalia, and hip joints. IMRT is particularly preferred for treating anal cancer due to its ability to concentrate radiation on the cancerous area while sparing nearby healthy structures, thereby minimizing side effects and improving treatment outcomes.
Relationships:
  - None listed in the provided data.</data>
