    <node id="LARYNGOSCOPY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">LARYNGOSCOPY is a scope-based examination of the larynx (voice box) and throat, specifically including the back of the throat and the hypopharynx (the area behind the voice box). It is performed using a laryngoscope and exists in several forms: indirect laryngoscopy, fiberoptic laryngoscopy, and direct laryngoscopy. These procedures fall under the general category of laryngoscopy and may also be included as part of a broader panendoscopy. Laryngoscopy is commonly used to evaluate the throat and voice box, particularly to look for tumors or other abnormalities in these areas.
Relationships:
  - (No direct relationships listed in the provided data for this entity)</data>
