    <node id="FERTILITY COUNSELING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">FERTILITY COUNSELING is a consultation process provided to individuals of all genders as part of overall treatment planning. It involves education and discussion about fertility preservation options and the potential fertility-related risks associated with a patient's proposed medical treatment. This counseling ensures that patients are informed about how their treatment may affect their reproductive health and what steps can be taken to preserve fertility for the future.
Relationships:
  - None listed</data>
