    <node id="PHOTODYNAMIC THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Photodynamic therapy (PDT) is a treatment option for actinic keratoses that uses light-activated therapy. In this approach, a light-sensitive drug is applied to the skin and becomes active when exposed to red or blue light, killing cancer cells. Common side effects of photodynamic therapy include itching, burning, pain, and redness.
Relationships:
  - Source: PHOTODYNAMIC THERAPY
  - Target: TOPICAL THERAPY
  - Description: Photodynamic therapy and topical therapy are both listed as treatment options for actinic keratoses.
  - Source: CRYOTHERAPY
  - Target: PHOTODYNAMIC THERAPY
  - Description: Cryotherapy and photodynamic therapy are both listed as treatment options for actinic keratoses.</data>
