    <node id="EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Extrafascial hysterectomy is a simple hysterectomy that removes only the uterus, including the cervix. It can be performed vaginally, abdominally, or using minimally invasive techniques. This procedure is used for the non-fertility-sparing treatment of certain early-stage cervical cancers, specifically including stage IA1 cancer.
