      <data key="d4">ENTITY: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
Description: Pelvic lymph node evaluation is a medical assessment of the lymph nodes located in the pelvic region, performed to determine whether cancer has spread from its primary site. Specifically, this evaluation is conducted as part of a radical hysterectomy for cervical cancer, allowing clinicians to examine the pelvic lymph nodes for signs of metastatic disease and thereby guide staging and treatment decisions.
Relationships:
  - Source: RADICAL TRACHELECTOMY
  - Target: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Description: Pelvic lymph node evaluation is performed along with radical trachelectomy
  - Source: MODIFIED RADICAL HYSTERECTOMY
  - Target: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Description: Pelvic lymph node evaluation is performed with modified radical hysterectomy
  - Source: RADICAL HYSTERECTOMY WITH PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Target: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Description: The procedure includes evaluation of pelvic lymph nodes
  - Source: LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Target: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Description: Pelvic lymph node evaluation is a type of lymph node evaluation
  - Source: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Target: PELVIC LYMPH NODE DISSECTION
  - Description: Pelvic lymph node dissection is a surgical form of pelvic lymph node evaluation
  - Source: HYSTERECTOMY
  - Target: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Description: Pelvic lymph nodes may be removed during hysterectomy
  - Source: CONE BIOPSY
  - Target: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Description: Pelvic lymph node evaluation is performed in addition to cone biopsy for certain stage 1 cancers
  - Source: EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY
  - Target: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Description: Pelvic lymph node evaluation is performed with extrafascial hysterectomy
  - Source: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Target: PARA-AORTIC LYMPH NODE REMOVAL
  - Description: Para-aortic lymph node removal may be performed in addition to pelvic lymph node evaluation</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING is a procedure performed before definitive treatment for cervical cancer, specifically when there is concern that the cancer has spread beyond the cervix. It involves the surgical removal and testing of pelvic and/or para-aortic lymph nodes to determine the extent of disease. This surgical evaluation guides treatment decisions by identifying whether metastasis has occurred. If cancer is found to have spread beyond the cervix, a hysterectomy is not performed, and alternative treatment approaches are pursued instead. The procedure thus serves as a critical diagnostic and staging step, enabling clinicians to tailor therapy based on the precise anatomical spread of the malignancy.
Relationships:
  - Source: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Target: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Description: Pre-treatment surgical staging is used to stage the extent of cervical cancer before treatment
  - Source: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Target: STAGING
  - Description: Pre-treatment surgical staging is a type of staging performed before treatment to assess cancer extent
  - Source: HYSTERECTOMY
  - Target: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Description: In cases where cervical cancer has spread beyond the cervix, a hysterectomy is not performed. Instead, pre-treatment surgical staging is considered to assess the extent of the disease. As part of this pre-treatment surgical staging, lymph nodes may be removed and tested to determine whether the cancer has spread to those nodes. This approach helps guide treatment decisions without proceeding to hysterectomy.
  - Source: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Target: LYMPH NODE REMOVAL
  - Description: Pre-treatment surgical staging may include removal of pelvic and/or para-aortic lymph nodes.
  - Source: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Target: LYMPH NODE TESTING
  - Description: Lymph nodes removed during pre-treatment surgical staging are tested to guide treatment decisions.
  - Source: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Target: PELVIC NODES
  - Description: Pre-treatment surgical staging may remove and test pelvic nodes.
  - Source: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Target: PARA-AORTIC NODES
  - Description: Pre-treatment surgical staging may remove and test para-aortic nodes.
  - Source: FIGO
  - Target: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Description: The FIGO system is used for staging cervical cancer before treatment
  - Source: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Target: LAPAROSCOPIC SURGICAL STAGING
  - Description: Laparoscopic surgical staging is a minimally invasive approach used to perform pre-treatment surgical staging.</data>
