    <node id="LYMPH NODE REMOVAL">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Lymph node removal is a surgical procedure in which one or more lymph nodes are excised for examination during pathologic staging. It involves the surgical removal of lymph nodes, including pelvic and para-aortic nodes, to help limit the spread of cancer cells and determine the extent of cancer.
Relationships:
  - Source: PATHOLOGIC STAGING
  - Target: LYMPH NODE REMOVAL
  - Description: Pathologic staging may examine a lymph node removed during surgery.
  - Source: PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING
  - Target: LYMPH NODE REMOVAL
  - Description: Pre-treatment surgical staging may include removal of pelvic and/or para-aortic lymph nodes.</data>
