    <node id="PARA-AORTIC LYMPH NODE REMOVAL">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Para-aortic lymph node removal is a surgical procedure that involves the excision of lymph nodes located in the abdomen, specifically around the aorta. This procedure is commonly performed to evaluate whether cancer has spread from its primary site to these lymph nodes. It is often carried out in addition to pelvic lymph node evaluation or as part of a broader surgical staging process. The primary purpose is to check for the presence of cancer cells, thereby helping to determine the extent of disease and guide subsequent treatment decisions.
Relationships:
  - Source: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Target: PARA-AORTIC LYMPH NODE REMOVAL
  - Description: Para-aortic lymph node removal may be performed in addition to pelvic lymph node evaluation
  - Source: RADICAL HYSTERECTOMY WITH PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Target: PARA-AORTIC LYMPH NODE REMOVAL
  - Description: Para-aortic lymph nodes may be removed in addition to pelvic lymph nodes during this procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
