    <node id="VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY is a form of radiation therapy in which brachytherapy is delivered through an applicator placed inside the vagina. It is specifically directed to the vaginal tissues and may be administered as part of a treatment plan that also includes external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) and platinum-based chemotherapy. This approach allows for targeted radiation to the vaginal region, often used to treat gynecologic malignancies.
Relationships:
  - Source: BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Target: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Description: Brachytherapy is a form of radiation therapy in which a radioactive source is placed inside or near the area requiring treatment. Vaginal brachytherapy is a specific type of brachytherapy that is applied directly to the vagina. In this procedure, a radioactive device is temporarily placed within the vaginal canal to deliver targeted radiation to the surrounding tissues. Vaginal brachytherapy is used to treat certain gynecological conditions, most commonly as part of the management of endometrial or vaginal cancers, often following surgery or external beam radiation. Because the radiation is delivered locally, it helps spare healthy surrounding organs from unnecessary exposure. Thus, vaginal brachytherapy is a subtype of the broader brachytherapy modality, distinguished by its anatomical site of delivery.
  - Source: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Target: CHEMORADIATION
  - Description: Vaginal brachytherapy may be added to chemoradiation
  - Source: EBRT
  - Target: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Description: Vaginal brachytherapy may be given in addition to EBRT and platinum chemotherapy
  - Source: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Target: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Vaginal brachytherapy may be given in addition to platinum chemotherapy
  - Source: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Description: Vaginal brachytherapy may be given in addition to EBRT and platinum chemotherapy
  - Source: EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)
  - Target: VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY
  - Description: Vaginal brachytherapy may be given in addition to EBRT</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
