    <node id="EASTERN COOPERATIVE ONCOLOGY GROUP">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) is a medical and cancer research organization best known for developing the ECOG performance status scale, also referred to as the ECOG performance status score or simply the ECOG score. This scale is used to rate a person's general level of fitness and ability to perform daily tasks, including self-care activities. In clinical practice, particularly in cancer care and treatment planning, the ECOG performance status provides a standardized measure of a patient's functional capacity, helping clinicians assess how well a patient can carry out everyday activities. The scale is widely utilized to guide treatment decisions, evaluate patient eligibility for therapies, and monitor changes in functional status over time. Overall, the ECOG performance status scale serves as an important tool for quantifying a patient's overall well-being and physical independence, with the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group being the organization credited with its development and widespread application.
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
