    <node id="PERMANENT COLOSTOMY">
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A permanent colostomy is a surgically created opening, known as a stoma, on the abdomen that allows stool to leave the body. This procedure is always required after an abdominoperineal resection (APR), and it is permanent, meaning the stoma is a lifelong necessity following this surgery.
Relationships:
  - Source: ABDOMINOPERINEAL RESECTION (APR)
  - Target: PERMANENT COLOSTOMY
  - Description: APR requires creating a permanent colostomy because the anus is removed
  - Source: ABDOMINOPERINEAL RESECTION
  - Target: PERMANENT COLOSTOMY
  - Description: APR always involves creating a permanent colostomy for stool to leave the body</data>
