  - Target: B-ALL
  - Description: The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides clinical practice guidelines that address the treatment of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia (B-ALL). Specifically, the NCCN Guidelines include a dedicated chapter on B-ALL treatment, and the NCCN Guidelines for Patients also contain a chapter covering this topic. These resources are designed to help healthcare professionals and patients understand evidence-based approaches to managing B-ALL, from diagnosis through treatment planning. The NCCN thus offers comprehensive, standardized guidance on B-ALL, ensuring that both clinical practitioners and patients have access to current, expert-reviewed information on therapeutic options for this disease.
  - Source: NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK
  - Target: BCR::ABL1-POSITIVE B-ALL
  - Description: The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides clinical guidance that includes a dedicated chapter on the treatment of BCR::ABL1-positive B-ALL. This information is presented in the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, which specifically address management and treatment options for this subtype of acute lymphoblastic leukemia.
  - Source: NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK
  - Target: BCR::ABL1-NEGATIVE OR BCR::ABL1-LIKE B-ALL
  - Description: The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides guidelines that include a chapter on BCR::ABL1-negative or BCR::ABL1-like B-ALL, which is identified as the most common type of B-ALL. The NCCN Guidelines for Patients also contain a chapter specifically addressing treatment for BCR::ABL1-negative or BCR::ABL1-like B-ALL, offering patient-focused information on managing this condition.
  - Source: NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK
