    <edge source="NCCN" target="HEAD AND NECK CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides patient-centered resources for individuals facing head and neck cancers. These offerings include patient guidelines specifically tailored to cancers of the head and neck region, as well as a dedicated Patient Guides for Cancer mobile app that delivers accessible information and guidance. The NCCNs patient information covers a broad range of malignancies in this anatomical area, with explicit inclusion of nasopharyngeal and oropharyngeal cancers, ensuring comprehensive education and support for patients navigating diagnosis, treatment, and survivorship.</data>
