    <edge source="NCCN" target="RECTAL CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">NCCN, the National Comprehensive Cancer Network, publishes patient-focused resources on rectal cancer. Specifically, NCCN makes available the NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Rectal Cancer, which are designed to provide patients with reliable, evidence-based information about the disease and its management. These guidelines translate the clinical NCCN Guidelines into plain language so that patients and caregivers can better understand rectal cancer treatment options, decision-making, and care planning. The publication is part of NCCN's broader mission to improve the quality and effectiveness of cancer care by ensuring patients have access to clear, expert-derived guidance. In summary, the entity NCCN is the publisher, and its patient guideline dedicated to rectal cancer is a key resource available to affected individuals and their families.</data>
      <data key="d8">RECTAL CANCER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN" target="IMMUNOTHERAPY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) offers patient education materials that describe immunotherapy as a type of systemic therapy. In its patient guidelines, NCCN provides detailed information on immunotherapy, including its side effects and the use of checkpoint inhibitors.</data>
      <data key="d8">IMMUNOTHERAPY</data>
    </edge>
