      <data key="d8">LOSS OF APPETITE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIATION THERAPY" target="PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Radiation therapy is a treatment used for primary CNS lymphoma, a cancer that affects the central nervous system. It is considered a main treatment option for this condition, playing a key role in managing the disease.</data>
      <data key="d8">PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIATION THERAPY" target="HEADACHES" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Headaches are a common side effect of radiation therapy</data>
      <data key="d8">HEADACHES</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIATION THERAPY" target="BRACHYTHERAPY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Brachytherapy is a type of radiation therapy. Specifically, it is a form of internal radiation therapy, meaning that radioactive material is placed directly inside the body. Radiation therapy is the broader category of treatment that uses radiation, and brachytherapy falls under this umbrella as an internal approach.</data>
      <data key="d8">BRACHYTHERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RADIATION THERAPY" target="WHOLE-BRAIN RADIATION THERAPY" id="0">
