    <edge source="SMOKEFREE.GOV" target="PATIENT" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">SmokeFree.gov is an online support resource for the patient to quit smoking or vaping</data>
      <data key="d8">PATIENT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SMOKEFREE.GOV" target="CDC" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">SmokeFree.gov and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) are both recognized as online support resources for individuals seeking to quit tobacco use. Specifically, SmokeFree.gov is listed as an online support option to help people quit smoking or vaping, while the CDC's website, CDC.gov/tobacco, is also listed as an online support resource for quitting tobacco. Together, they serve as accessible digital tools for tobacco cessation, offering guidance and assistance to those looking to stop using tobacco products.</data>
      <data key="d8">CDC</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SMOKEFREE.GOV" target="BETOBACCOFREE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
