      <data key="d8">CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ECHOCARDIOGRAM" target="ULTRASOUND" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">An echocardiogram is a type of ultrasound. Specifically, an echocardiogram is an ultrasound procedure that uses sound waves to create pictures of the heart. In this context, ultrasound refers both to the broader imaging modality and to the technology that employs high-frequency sound waves to visualize internal structures. The echocardiogram, as a specialized application of ultrasound, focuses on the heart, allowing healthcare providers to examine its structure and function in detail. Together, these descriptions establish that the echocardiogram is a subset of ultrasound, distinguished by its use of sound waves to generate images of the heart.</data>
      <data key="d8">ECHOCARDIOGRAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ELECTROCARDIOGRAM (ECG OR EKG)" target="ECHOCARDIOGRAM" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both are heart tests, but ECG measures electrical activity while echocardiogram images heart structure</data>
      <data key="d8">ECHOCARDIOGRAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ULTRASOUND" target="IMAGING TESTS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Ultrasound is an imaging test.</data>
      <data key="d8">ULTRASOUND</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ULTRASOUND" target="BIOPSY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Ultrasound is an imaging technique that can be used to guide a biopsy procedure, helping clinicians target the correct area for tissue sampling. It is commonly utilized to guide biopsies of the prostate, and may also be used to guide biopsies in other clinical contexts.</data>
      <data key="d8">ULTRASOUND</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ULTRASOUND" target="IMAGING" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Ultrasound is an imaging procedure.</data>
      <data key="d8">ULTRASOUND</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ULTRASOUND" target="MRI" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">MRI may be used if the ultrasound images are unclear.</data>
      <data key="d8">ULTRASOUND</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ULTRASOUND" target="CT SCAN" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both are imaging modalities that can be used to guide a biopsy.</data>
      <data key="d8">ULTRASOUND</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ULTRASOUND" target="LIVER CANCER" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Ultrasound is used in liver cancer screening to detect abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d8">ULTRASOUND</data>
    </edge>
