    </edge>
    <edge source="PREMATURE MENOPAUSE" target="HORMONE REPLACEMENT THERAPY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Hormone replacement therapy may be suggested to manage symptoms of premature/surgical menopause</data>
      <data key="d8">PREMATURE MENOPAUSE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OVARY PRESERVATION" target="SURGICAL MENOPAUSE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Preserving the ovaries during hysterectomy prevents surgical menopause from removal of both ovaries</data>
      <data key="d8">SURGICAL MENOPAUSE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OVARY PRESERVATION" target="MENOPAUSE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Preserving the ovaries prevents the sudden drop in estrogen that would cause menopause</data>
      <data key="d8">OVARY PRESERVATION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MENOPAUSE" target="SURGICAL MENOPAUSE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Menopause is the natural biological transition marking the end of a woman's reproductive years; however, not all menopause occurs naturally. Surgical menopause is a distinct form of menopause caused by surgery. As the descriptions indicate, surgical menopause is a type of menopause that arises specifically as a result of a surgical procedure, rather than through the body's natural hormonal decline. Thus, within the broader category of menopause, surgical menopause is defined by its surgical origin, distinguishing it from spontaneous or naturally occurring menopause. Both descriptions provided are consistent, with no contradictions to resolve: surgical menopause is simply menopause that is induced by surgery. Therefore, it is recognized as a valid and specific subtype of menopause, unified under the same overarching biological condition but differing in its cause.</data>
      <data key="d8">SURGICAL MENOPAUSE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MENOPAUSE" target="SUDDEN DROP IN ESTROGEN" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">A sudden drop in estrogen causes the symptoms of menopause when menopause is caused by surgery</data>
      <data key="d8">SUDDEN DROP IN ESTROGEN</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MENOPAUSE" target="PREMATURE MENOPAUSE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Premature menopause is early menopause.</data>
      <data key="d8">PREMATURE MENOPAUSE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MENOPAUSE" target="RADIATION-INDUCED MENOPAUSE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
